FIX THE REGRESSION (1-line change). In /app/frontend/lib/i18n.ts at the bottom of `initI18n()` (just before `return chosen;` on line 83), add a listener notification so React subscribers update from the module-default to the actually-loaded locale: 

  try {
    i18n.locale = chosen;
    listeners.forEach((cb) => { try { cb(chosen); } catch {} });
  } catch {}
  return chosen;

This preserves the defensive refactor (still does NOT call I18nManager.forceRTL on first mount, which was the actual reason for the refactor) while restoring listener notification. Verified locally that without this, picker is stuck showing FR-active when storage is non-FR.
